# Android Development

A clean, professional repository for Android development experiments, practice apps, and learning projects.

## Overview
This repository stores Android development work, including UI layouts, app logic, and project-based learning exercises. The goal is to keep the codebase organized, easy to navigate, and ready for future expansion.

## Features
- Android app development examples
- Learning-focused project structure
- Clean setup for future improvements
- Organized source files and project artifacts

## Prerequisites
- Android Studio
- JDK 17 or newer
- Android SDK
- Git

## Getting Started
1. Clone the repository:
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/javaidgithub/Android-Development.git
   ```
2. Open the project in Android Studio.
3. Sync Gradle files.
4. Build or run the app using an emulator or connected device.

## Project Structure
```text
Android-Development/
├── app/
├── gradle/
├── .gitignore
├── README.md
├── LICENSE
└── settings.gradle
```

